WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:36.730
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:37.000 --> 00:38.000
Ouch!

3
01:33.170 --> 01:34.170
Good morning.

4
01:37.860 --> 01:38.860
Smells so good.

5
01:48.560 --> 01:51.140
Isn't it a hassle to make pour-over coffee every time?

6
01:52.610 --> 01:55.810
How about I buy you a coffee maker to cover my rent?

7
01:56.900 --> 02:00.770
No thanks, I like doing it this way.

8
02:06.220 --> 02:07.220
More importantly,

9
02:08.640 --> 02:10.240
don't just crawl into my bed.

10
02:10.900 --> 02:13.400
It's a double bed anyway, what's the big deal?

11
02:14.280 --> 02:15.720
That's not the point.

12
02:17.880 --> 02:18.980
What's this?

13
02:21.960 --> 02:23.590
Got it on sale for cheap.

14
02:26.120 --> 02:28.360
And here you are, doing the exact same thing.

15
02:29.120 --> 02:30.120
Shut up.

16
02:32.270 --> 02:35.500
I heard it's really soothing, or rather, great for stress relief.

17
02:46.250 --> 02:47.250
Kanda.

18
02:49.720 --> 02:51.740
Seriously, stop crawling into my bed.

19
02:56.600 --> 02:59.520
Get up! We're gonna be late.

20
02:59.960 --> 03:00.960
Hmm...

21
03:08.730 --> 03:11.850
Ueno, can I go to work with you today?

22
03:15.340 --> 03:16.340
Are you serious?

23
03:17.240 --> 03:19.530
Some people at work know I'm gay.

24
03:19.570 --> 03:22.020
Didn't I tell you not to talk to me so much at the office?

25
03:23.520 --> 03:24.520
Yeah, yeah.

26
03:24.830 --> 03:27.400
Still, we can at least take the train together, right?

27
04:27.140 --> 04:29.560
"You Should Be The One To Come Kiss Me"

28
04:30.640 --> 04:31.729
(Episode 2)

29
04:31.730 --> 04:33.530
A Sales Department dinner?

30
04:33.860 --> 04:34.860
Yes...

31
04:35.480 --> 04:37.820
It's next Monday.

32
04:39.100 --> 04:40.260
Would you be able to make it?

33
04:40.680 --> 04:42.640
Is it okay for me to go, since I'm in Accounting?

34
04:43.440 --> 04:46.110
It's also to celebrate Sales landing a big client.

35
04:46.200 --> 04:49.680
We're inviting people from other departments too, so if you're free...

36
04:50.540 --> 04:52.500
There's still a miscalculation here.

37
04:53.920 --> 04:54.990
Sorry.

38
04:58.710 --> 04:59.950
I appreciate the invite, but...

39
05:00.040 --> 05:01.040
Oh.

40
05:02.280 --> 05:04.960
It's a team appreciation dinner, so it's on the company, of course.

41
05:05.180 --> 05:06.180
I'm in.

42
05:11.460 --> 05:12.460
I'm back.

43
05:12.700 --> 05:13.960
Good work, everyone.

44
05:14.980 --> 05:16.959
Shirai, is the proposal ready?

45
05:16.960 --> 05:17.960
All done.

46
05:18.800 --> 05:19.800
Oh, thanks.

47
05:20.920 --> 05:23.580
I invited Ueno-san to the dinner, too.

48
05:24.300 --> 05:26.376
He said yes the second you mentioned it's on the company, right?

49
05:26.400 --> 05:28.280
Yep! Worked like a charm.

50
05:28.440 --> 05:29.440
Told you.

51
05:33.200 --> 05:36.050
Are you and Ueno-san close, Kanda-san?

52
05:37.500 --> 05:38.530
Yeah.

53
05:42.380 --> 05:44.920
Didn't I tell you not to talk to me so much at the office?

54
05:46.050 --> 05:47.450
I wouldn't say we're on good terms.

55
05:47.500 --> 05:48.700
Well, which is it?

56
05:58.230 --> 05:59.500
About Ueno-san...

57
06:02.280 --> 06:03.280
Hmm?

58
06:05.980 --> 06:06.980
Never mind.

59
06:07.300 --> 06:09.460
There are rumors that you two don't get along,

60
06:10.500 --> 06:12.520
so I was just curious which one was true.

61
06:13.820 --> 06:15.250
Huh? People are saying that?

62
06:18.670 --> 06:19.920
Forget I said anything.

63
06:21.880 --> 06:22.980
Too late for that.

64
06:23.480 --> 06:24.590
Now it's gonna bug me.

65
06:24.760 --> 06:25.880
- Shirai. - Yes?

66
06:26.400 --> 06:27.606
- Kobayashi? - You just bumped into me.

67
06:27.630 --> 06:29.380
Hold on a sec, Shirai.

68
06:40.770 --> 06:42.210
Are you having lunch here too, Ueno?

69
06:46.060 --> 06:48.940
Would you be happy getting puffed corn snacks and dried squid as a gift?

70
06:50.780 --> 06:51.780
Sure.

71
06:52.060 --> 06:53.480
Those corn snacks are pretty good.

72
06:55.040 --> 06:57.360
Even as a promotion gift for a friend?

73
06:58.220 --> 06:59.220
What?

74
06:59.320 --> 07:01.400
Then you should definitely get them something nicer.

75
07:04.290 --> 07:05.830
He's the one who asked for it.

76
07:08.780 --> 07:10.480
What is he, a high schooler?

77
07:11.420 --> 07:14.670
Isn't it best to just get him what he wants?

78
07:15.260 --> 07:16.260
True.

79
07:17.020 --> 07:19.883
Getting something that isn't aligned with your taste can be kind of a pain.

80
07:26.223 --> 07:27.240
What's wrong?

81
08:06.730 --> 08:10.450
Any updates on that wish list?

82
08:15.420 --> 08:18.260
Please let me know if there's any progress.

83
08:36.260 --> 08:37.360
Congrats.

84
08:43.420 --> 08:44.520
Huh?

85
08:44.620 --> 08:46.980
Don't tell me you're trying to brush this off.

86
08:50.530 --> 08:51.530
Maybe.

87
08:58.860 --> 09:01.490
Are you limiting yourself to one-word replies or something?

88
09:07.330 --> 09:08.500
Annoying.

89
09:58.340 --> 09:59.340
Welcome.

90
10:12.240 --> 10:14.060
Are you looking for a tie?

91
10:16.000 --> 10:17.000
Um...

92
10:22.490 --> 10:24.030
I'm buying one for a friend.

93
10:25.080 --> 10:26.810
Would it be weird to give a tie as a gift?

94
10:27.180 --> 10:29.060
No, not at all.

95
10:29.620 --> 10:33.710
Many customers buy them to celebrate promotions or birthdays.

96
10:34.760 --> 10:35.980
I see...

97
10:36.080 --> 10:37.080
Yes.

98
10:50.350 --> 10:52.019
Let's pool our strength together

99
10:52.043 --> 10:54.383
and take on even greater challenges.

100
10:58.380 --> 11:00.569
Now, let's have the project leader,

101
11:00.570 --> 11:03.800
Kanda-san from Sales, say a few words and lead the toast.

102
11:06.620 --> 11:07.620
Thank you.

103
11:08.100 --> 11:10.820
Thank you for the introduction. I'm Kanda from the Sales Department.

104
11:12.320 --> 11:14.080
Just as Department Manager Tabata mentioned,

105
11:14.290 --> 11:16.720
the real test for this project starts now.

106
11:16.980 --> 11:19.550
With everyone's help, I hope we can

107
11:19.630 --> 11:23.250
- build new relationships of trust... - Ueno, you made it.

108
11:23.470 --> 11:24.560
Thank goodness.

109
11:24.880 --> 11:26.480
I'm the only one here from PR.

110
11:26.760 --> 11:27.960
Same for me from Accounting.

111
11:28.760 --> 11:30.830
We're kind of out of place here, huh?

112
11:37.480 --> 11:38.880
Looking for someone?

113
11:38.900 --> 11:39.920
Nope.

114
11:41.360 --> 11:43.250
Isn't Kanda dragging this out a bit?

115
11:43.740 --> 11:45.380
He literally just started.

116
11:52.260 --> 11:55.040
I think I'll go grab a drink, too.

117
12:03.390 --> 12:04.550
Excuse me...

118
12:05.100 --> 12:07.170
Sorry, can I order a drink right now?

119
12:07.800 --> 12:08.800
Here.

120
12:10.040 --> 12:11.040
Oolong tea, right?

121
12:14.610 --> 12:15.390
Thanks.

122
12:15.520 --> 12:18.200
I look forward to working with you all and appreciate your support.

123
12:18.300 --> 12:20.810
That said, if I keep talking business like this,

124
12:20.860 --> 12:23.070
the manager might chew me out,

125
12:24.240 --> 12:26.840
so I'll wrap it up here.

126
12:28.060 --> 12:30.360
Does everyone have a drink?

127
12:30.980 --> 12:34.040
By the way, we have people from other departments joining us tonight,

128
12:34.170 --> 12:36.690
so let's use this chance to mingle...

129
12:38.340 --> 12:39.340
All right.

130
12:39.700 --> 12:41.010
I know that was a bit short,

131
12:42.240 --> 12:45.580
but it sounds like Shirai is starving.

132
12:45.780 --> 12:46.960
Did everyone hear that?

133
12:47.040 --> 12:48.580
All right, let's do the toast!

134
12:49.100 --> 12:50.840
Glasses up, everyone.

135
12:51.560 --> 12:52.560
Here we go.

136
12:52.980 --> 12:55.560
- Cheers! - Cheers!

137
12:57.180 --> 12:58.180
Thank you.

138
12:58.980 --> 12:59.980
Thanks.

139
13:00.110 --> 13:01.780
Great job.

140
13:08.620 --> 13:11.290
- You've been working really hard. - It's all thanks to you, boss.

141
13:11.500 --> 13:12.699
Sorry to always trouble you.

142
13:12.700 --> 13:14.180
Let's not talk about work at a party.

143
13:14.420 --> 13:15.520
I'm really sorry.

144
13:15.593 --> 13:17.772
Still, the deadline's tomorrow, so I'm counting on you.

145
13:17.822 --> 13:18.563
Tomorrow?

146
13:19.360 --> 13:20.920
Want to grab a drink together sometime?

147
13:22.760 --> 13:24.520
We haven't gone out for drinks yet, have we?

148
13:25.640 --> 13:26.640
Right?

149
13:28.100 --> 13:28.900
Are you listening?

150
13:28.900 --> 13:29.900
To what I just said.

151
13:30.360 --> 13:31.520
Are you even listening to me?

152
13:31.600 --> 13:32.500
Yeah, I'm listening.

153
13:32.501 --> 13:33.700
Good, good.

154
13:34.400 --> 13:35.400
Sorry for the wait.

155
13:35.480 --> 13:37.230
Great, thank you.

156
13:39.660 --> 13:40.860
Whoa, what's up with you?

157
13:41.100 --> 13:42.340
Oh, you're here too, Mizoguchi.

158
13:46.740 --> 13:47.740
Are you okay?

159
13:48.280 --> 13:49.280
Is that alcohol?

160
13:49.910 --> 13:51.330
No, it's oolong tea...

161
13:53.560 --> 13:54.560
Hey!

162
13:58.260 --> 14:00.520
This isn't an oolong highball, right?

163
14:10.400 --> 14:11.560
So pointless...

164
14:14.040 --> 14:15.079
What's wrong?

165
14:15.080 --> 14:16.080
Did something happen?

166
14:18.580 --> 14:19.580
No idea.

167
14:23.230 --> 14:25.350
Have you seen Ueno?

168
14:28.340 --> 14:29.340
Who knows.

169
14:32.370 --> 14:33.370
Ah.

170
14:39.460 --> 14:41.080
Congrats on landing the big client.

171
14:43.960 --> 14:44.960
Thanks...

172
14:54.720 --> 14:55.720
Ueno-san.

173
14:55.930 --> 14:58.050
- Oh, hey. - Good work today.

174
14:58.690 --> 15:01.000
It's rare to see you at a gathering like this.

175
15:01.400 --> 15:02.400
Yeah.

176
15:03.040 --> 15:04.400
I'm just here for the free dinner.

177
15:05.360 --> 15:06.390
Same here.

178
15:10.540 --> 15:11.540
Um...

179
15:12.680 --> 15:14.780
Sorry Shirai is always giving you a hard time.

180
15:16.790 --> 15:19.880
His epic miscalculations are honestly kind of impressive at this point.

181
15:21.580 --> 15:22.780
"Epic," huh?

182
15:23.660 --> 15:25.480
I'm gonna start calling him that.

183
15:33.200 --> 15:35.590
This might be a little out of nowhere,

184
15:39.310 --> 15:40.820
but I'm actually gay, too.

185
15:42.560 --> 15:43.580
Are you okay?

186
15:44.540 --> 15:45.630
You didn't know?

187
15:46.340 --> 15:48.360
I'm pretty open about it.

188
15:49.320 --> 15:50.320
No, it's just...

189
15:51.280 --> 15:52.720
That completely caught me off guard.

190
15:53.410 --> 15:54.410
Sorry about that.

191
15:55.800 --> 15:56.800
It's fine.

192
15:57.140 --> 15:58.140
I don't really mind.

193
15:59.380 --> 16:02.470
I heard you were gay too, Ueno-san.

194
16:03.160 --> 16:04.160
Yeah...

195
16:05.360 --> 16:06.360
I see.

196
16:08.710 --> 16:09.760
Have you told

197
16:10.380 --> 16:11.580
anyone around you?

198
16:13.590 --> 16:14.590
No.

199
16:15.180 --> 16:17.260
Just a few people who joined the company in my year.

200
16:17.440 --> 16:18.440
Gotcha.

201
16:20.460 --> 16:21.800
Huh? Kobayashi,

202
16:22.220 --> 16:23.740
are you and Ueno-san close?

203
16:24.230 --> 16:26.060
Is there a problem if we are?

204
16:26.380 --> 16:27.580
I didn't say that.

205
16:28.960 --> 16:31.626
Ueno-san, you and Kanda-san joined the company in the same year, right?

206
16:31.650 --> 16:32.770
Wait, how is that, honestly?

207
16:32.990 --> 16:34.190
Doesn't it feel a bit awkward?

208
16:34.950 --> 16:37.869
Starting at the same time as someone as amazing as Kanda-san...

209
16:37.870 --> 16:39.290
must be really tough on you.

210
16:39.820 --> 16:42.700
Well, you're in accounting now, so maybe it doesn't matter.

211
16:42.960 --> 16:45.250
Jeez, stop saying such rude things.

212
16:46.020 --> 16:47.320
I'm so sorry, Ueno-san.

213
16:47.580 --> 16:49.080
This guy has no filter.

214
16:49.420 --> 16:50.390
It's fine...

215
16:50.420 --> 16:52.580
Besides, the two of them get along great.

216
16:53.140 --> 16:54.570
Stop making up your own narrative.

217
16:55.180 --> 16:56.180
Oh, really?

218
16:56.200 --> 17:00.700
I actually saw them walking to work together the other day.

219
17:01.000 --> 17:02.000
That's surprising.

220
17:02.520 --> 17:04.040
I had no idea you two were that close.

221
17:04.900 --> 17:06.780
Sorry for just blurting that out.

222
17:07.160 --> 17:10.580
He just kept making weird assumptions about you two.

223
17:10.880 --> 17:13.400
- He has a terrible personality. Even before... - That's not it.

224
17:13.490 --> 17:14.490
Huh?

225
17:14.740 --> 17:18.340
That was just a coincidence. He and I aren't particularly close.

226
17:19.140 --> 17:20.860
It's not like we're on bad terms, though.

227
17:22.700 --> 17:23.700
It's just...

228
17:24.600 --> 17:27.720
since we started the same year, we chat occasionally. That's really all it is.

229
17:28.420 --> 17:30.460
It's not like we're best friends or anything.

230
17:32.260 --> 17:33.260
I see...

231
17:33.960 --> 17:36.589
I'm so sorry for saying such weird things!

232
17:36.590 --> 17:38.739
- Let's go already! - See? I knew it was a touchy subject.

233
17:38.740 --> 17:40.630
Knock it off and let's go!

234
17:49.940 --> 17:50.940
Alright, next stop...

235
17:51.620 --> 17:58.410
the skewer place for round two!

236
17:58.740 --> 18:01.030
I'm in! I can drink till sunrise. Who's with me?

237
18:01.080 --> 18:04.290
- Are you going? - Let's go!

238
18:06.420 --> 18:08.300
Kanda, you're coming to the after-party, right?

239
18:08.580 --> 18:09.580
Oh, sure.

240
18:09.720 --> 18:10.920
I'll be there.

241
18:12.340 --> 18:13.510
Excuse me.

242
18:22.890 --> 18:23.890
Found you.

243
18:24.240 --> 18:25.240
Thank goodness.

244
18:29.700 --> 18:31.120
Can I come over to your place now?

245
18:31.660 --> 18:32.760
Let's have another drink.

246
18:35.860 --> 18:36.860
Oh, right.

247
18:37.280 --> 18:38.280
My bad.

248
18:39.200 --> 18:41.120
Doing things like this is the problem, isn't it?

249
18:41.660 --> 18:42.660
Huh?

250
18:44.700 --> 18:47.640
I overheard what Nakagawa-san said earlier.

251
18:48.860 --> 18:50.580
She saw us the other morning, didn't she?

252
18:51.820 --> 18:52.820
I'm sorry.

253
18:53.900 --> 18:55.220
I'll be more careful from now on.

254
19:02.400 --> 19:03.780
It's not your fault.

255
19:06.100 --> 19:09.030
I'm just being overly paranoid.

256
19:11.230 --> 19:12.230
I'm sorry.

257
19:15.940 --> 19:16.940
I see.

258
19:18.980 --> 19:21.050
Well, there's a lot to consider.

259
19:32.000 --> 19:33.870
So, can I still come over?

260
19:37.260 --> 19:38.260
Sure, you can.

261
19:39.300 --> 19:40.700
What about the after-party, though?

262
19:41.360 --> 19:42.360
Oh.

263
19:42.760 --> 19:45.400
Everyone's pretty wasted already. They won't even notice I'm gone.

264
19:47.640 --> 19:48.640
In that case...

265
19:49.000 --> 19:50.560
let's grab some drinks on the way back.

266
19:51.350 --> 19:52.350
Okay.

267
20:06.910 --> 20:08.800
The night breeze feels so nice.

268
20:15.980 --> 20:16.980
Oh!

269
20:17.260 --> 20:18.460
Let's have hot pot next time.

270
20:19.480 --> 20:21.066
Since we went to the trouble of buying that pot.

271
20:21.090 --> 20:22.360
I'm craving offal hot pot.

272
20:23.740 --> 20:25.960
What kind do you want, Ueno?

273
20:45.560 --> 20:46.560
Well...

274
20:48.370 --> 20:49.370
Wait, if...

275
20:50.300 --> 20:52.060
- If it's a bother for you... - Kanda.

276
21:02.260 --> 21:03.260
Here.

277
21:05.260 --> 21:06.260
Huh?

278
21:06.850 --> 21:07.850
A congratulatory gift.

279
21:18.840 --> 21:21.000
I was going to wait until your promotion was official.

280
21:21.660 --> 21:22.780
But I was afraid I'd forget.

281
21:22.920 --> 21:25.176
Or one of us might suddenly get transferred or something.

282
21:25.200 --> 21:26.720
Just sell it if you don't want it.

283
21:28.240 --> 21:30.200
You don't have to use it...

284
21:35.670 --> 21:36.670
Wait...

285
21:37.000 --> 21:38.160
You're opening it right here?

286
21:40.260 --> 21:41.260
It's a tie...

287
21:45.540 --> 21:48.160
That's what you get for sending me such a half-hearted wishlist.

288
21:49.360 --> 21:51.240
So I just picked one based on my own taste.

289
21:53.020 --> 21:56.060
I don't know what people usually go for, so don't complain.

290
22:02.040 --> 22:03.040
Ueno...

291
22:06.260 --> 22:07.260
Thank you.

292
22:08.600 --> 22:09.600
I'm so happy.

293
22:17.200 --> 22:18.250
Well? How is it?

294
22:19.920 --> 22:20.920
Does it look good?

295
22:23.380 --> 22:24.380
Yeah.

296
22:26.300 --> 22:27.820
Sorry I just went with my own taste...

297
22:28.960 --> 22:31.320
You picked it out, Ueno, so I know it looks great.

298
22:32.200 --> 22:33.260
Oh, but...

299
22:34.900 --> 22:36.780
I still want to see how it looks in the mirror.

300
22:38.400 --> 22:39.500
Let's hurry back.

301
22:40.680 --> 22:41.680
Yeah.

302
22:44.560 --> 22:45.560
Let's go.

303
22:46.150 --> 22:47.790
I want to see the happy look on his face.

304
22:49.200 --> 22:53.860
Because he works so hard every day, I want to give him something special from time to time.

305
22:57.080 --> 22:58.180
Moments like these...

306
22:58.920 --> 23:00.180
more than anyone else...

307
23:00.960 --> 23:02.960
I want to be the one he shares them with the most.

308
23:18.920 --> 23:20.150
There I go again...

309
24:14.780 --> 24:17.030
(Next Episode Preview) What do I even want anymore?

310
24:17.380 --> 24:19.760
Isn't being able to sleep together the first hurdle?

311
24:20.040 --> 24:21.490
You're not even my type.

312
24:21.670 --> 24:24.280
Nothing is ever going to happen between us.

313
24:24.700 --> 24:28.580
I guess that's what you'd call friends with benefits.
